(6703016, 1001519, 141542, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Tiny:</b></div><hr/><i> Still my fav of the lot and think we need more shots of your lovely wife. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m flattered by you finding this to be so good.<br/> <br/>As for her future appearances, don''t worry about that, so far, she''s the only model I have!  (And I don''t mind that one bit...although..she might a little hahaha)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-03-07 15:14:21.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Tiny: Still my fav of the lot and think we need more shots of your lovely wife.   I''m flattered by you finding this to be so good. As for her future appearances, don''t worry about that, so far, she''s the only model I have!  (And I don''t mind that one bit...although..she might a little hahaha)', '2012-03-07 15:13:27.000000', '2012-03-07 15:14:21.000000', 0),
(6703232, 1001573, 97225, '<td valign="top">You already have an amazing range of faces. One of the strengths of your self-portrait collection is due to your ability to present yourself differently every time. And changing your name won''t help a bit as voters don''t see that until after voting - except when you Semperfy your title it is possible that you COULD give the game away, LOL. :-)</td>', 'You already have an amazing range of faces. One of the strengths of your self-portrait collection is due to your ability to present yourself differently every time. And changing your name won''t help a bit as voters don''t see that until after voting - except when you Semperfy your title it is possible that you COULD give the game away, LOL. :-)', '2012-03-07 17:03:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6703341, 1001519, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is a cute shot and glad I gave you a 7 in voting :-)  Your wife is gorgeous, the details are spot on, and knowing (in hindsight of course) that there actually is a bun in the oven just adds to the sweetness of your final placing and the delight on her face.  Not a lot to nitpick here apart from the lighting, either another light or at least a reflector on the right to light her face.  It is a little distracting but I think in this case the one-sided lighting works in its own way.  My own oven''s light is set off to one side so it doesn''t look that fake to me.  Good dof and glad you did go with the highish ISO, it paid off.<br/> <br/>I too would actually like to have seen an actual bun of some sort in the oven, just in the lower third.  My own significant other thinks a pizza arcing from one corner to the other would have made this image even better.  But there''s nothing better than getting a new PB with your favourite person in the frame.<br/> <br/>So congratulations - for both reasons - and keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is a cute shot and glad I gave you a 7 in voting :-)  Your wife is gorgeous, the details are spot on, and knowing (in hindsight of course) that there actually is a bun in the oven just adds to the sweetness of your final placing and the delight on her face.  Not a lot to nitpick here apart from the lighting, either another light or at least a reflector on the right to light her face.  It is a little distracting but I think in this case the one-sided lighting works in its own way.  My own oven''s light is set off to one side so it doesn''t look that fake to me.  Good dof and glad you did go with the highish ISO, it paid off. I too would actually like to have seen an actual bun of some sort in the oven, just in the lower third.  My own significant other thinks a pizza arcing from one corner to the other would have made this image even better.  But there''s nothing better than getting a new PB with your favourite person in the frame. So congratulations - for both reasons - and keep up the good work! Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-03-07 18:38:48.000000', NULL, 0),
